-- Do not edit by hand: change the spec and regenerate.
--
-- ROOT CAUSE
--
-- Migration 1054 multiplied the hammer blow energy by materialTypeFactor's impact energy factor as well as by the material's own
-- flow stress. That factor is the material's flow stress relative to carbon steel (stainless 0.59, aluminium 2.68, titanium and
-- Inconel 0.47), so the material was counted twice and the wrong way round: a magnesium forging needed more blow energy than the
-- same part in Inconel. The energy is now the deformation work at the material's own flow stress, times the plant's adjustment.
--
-- This migration creates one global calculator per spec entry (inputs are the
-- values the cost engine seeds, each shown with its source in the calculation
-- trace; calculated fields are the formulas the engine evaluates, it holds
-- none) and links every Forging catalog operation it computes to its
-- calculator in process_calculator_mappings.
--
-- Requires migration 804 (calculators.retired_at).
-- Self-contained, idempotent, post-checked.

BEGIN;

-- Forging - Hammer energy
